Feasibility Study – General Overview
Here is the key areas we will explore in the feasibility study for our Plant Disease Detection App. The goal is to understand the current situation in Jordan, identify opportunities, and highlight what our AI-powered solution can improve. 

1. Current Methods Used in Jordan 
• Farmers usually rely on personal experience or advice from neighboring farmers. 
• Many contact agricultural engineers through cooperatives or pay for field visits. 
• Some use WhatsApp groups to send photos and ask for help. 
• Diagnosis often comes late due to limited access to experts. 
• Pesticides are sometimes used randomly without proper identification of the disease. 
These methods are slow, inconsistent, and can lead to crop loss or unnecessary chemical use. 

2. How Our App Could Make an Impact 

• Instant diagnosis using AI from a simple photo. 
• Early detection helps prevent large-scale crop damage. 
• Reduces cost by minimizing unnecessary pesticide use and repeated expert visits. 
• Saves time by eliminating delays in receiving guidance. 
• Provides consistent information and supports farmers in remote or underserved areas. 
• Helps farmers make more informed decisions, improving overall productivity and yield. 

